    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS`, test green. Here's how I addressed the review.\n\n## Finding 1 \u2014 `maxMemberLevel` mutating other owners (agreed, fixed)\n\nThe hidden `other.setHouseholdSize(...)` inside the `mapToInt` is gone. `maxMemberLevel` is now a pure read: for each other household member it computes `MembershipLevel.level(MembershipLevel.points(other, sizeIn(other, counts)))`, where `sizeIn` is a pure lookup against the pre-computed counts. No entity is mutated during the max computation, and no ordering dependency on a prior stamping pass remains \u2014 so I didn't need the two-pass restructure the review suggested as one option; removing the shared-mutable-state entirely is simpler and achieves the same goal.\n\n## Finding 2 \u2014 `OwnerHousehold` depending on `OwnerMapper` (agreed, took the suggested direction)\n\nRather than have the upstream stamper reach into the downstream mapper, I extracted the points\u2192level formula into a small shared unit, `MembershipLevel` (alongside the existing `IdentityKey`/`HouseholdKey`/`CustomerCode` helpers in the same package):\n\n- `points(Owner, Integer householdSize)` \u2014 household size passed in explicitly (no reading the transient field), keeping it a pure function.\n- `level(int points)` \u2014 raw level from points.\n\nNow:\n- `OwnerMapper` delegates (`membershipPoints`, `rawMembershipLevel`, `hasEmail` all call into `MembershipLevel`); its public API and DTO mappings are unchanged.\n- `OwnerHousehold` no longer depends on `OwnerMapper` \u2014 its constructor is back to just `OwnerRepository`, and it computes members' raw levels directly from the shared unit. The layering inversion is eliminated.\n\nI also cleaned up the now-unused `FiscalYear`/`LocalDate` imports in the mapper (they only appear inside MapStruct expression strings, which are fully qualified).\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged \u2014 the formula and the capping logic produce identical results; only the code's structure moved. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
